problem:
Consider the family of parabolas defined by \( y = (x-h)^2 \) for \( h \in \mathbb{R} \) (moving the vertex to various x-coordinates) and the line \( y = 4x + k \) (with constant slope 4 and varying y-intercept \( k \)). For a given integer \( h \), how many fixed real values of \( k \) will make the following value a real number?

\[ g^{-1}(h) := \dfrac{2 \sqrt{5}}{\sqrt{k}} - 4 \sqrt{\dfrac{5}k} + 4 h \]

\boxed{-12 \pm 4\sqrt{15}}
